1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:05,510
What if the ships simply stopped coming… and the only man left on your island became the monster?

2
00:00:05,530 --> 00:00:16,170
Clipperton: a speck of coral more than a thousand kilometers from Acapulco. In the early 1900s, Mexican soldiers and their families lived there, under Captain Ramón Arnaud.

3
00:00:16,190 --> 00:00:23,610
They depended on supply ships. Then, as revolution tore through Mexico, the ships stopped coming. Food ran out. Scurvy spread.

4
00:00:23,630 --> 00:00:29,550
When a ship appeared on the horizon, Arnaud and the last soldiers rowed out to reach it. They never came back.

5
00:00:29,570 --> 00:00:37,660
Only one grown man was left among the women and children: the lighthouse keeper, Victoriano Álvarez. He declared himself king of Clipperton.

6
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:43,870
Survivors described rape, beatings, and murder. There was nowhere to run. Beyond the beach, there was only ocean.

7
00:00:43,890 --> 00:00:49,160
On July 18, 1917, Alicia Arnaud and Tirza Rendón killed him.

8
00:00:49,180 --> 00:01:00,893
That same day, the USS Yorktown appeared on a wartime patrol. It hadn't come for them. Eleven survivors went home. Help arrived the very day they stopped waiting for it. This is Plot Twist with A&R.

